        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33988779?u=5b5fc67c907002674087c98a6503db95c41b6245&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I would like to request a feature for the use of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matroska\" rel=\"nofollow\">Matroska video container</a> (also called MKV) in <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;video&gt;</code> tags.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From my testing, it is supported in the latest versions of Chromium and GNOME Web (WebKit-based), but not in the latest version of Firefox.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">WebM is based on MKV, but they are not the same format - WebM is already provided as a feature on caniuse.com, and support is present in latest versions of all major browsers.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here's a page I made so I could test support myself: <a href=\"https://grzesiek11.stary.pc.pl/files/mkv.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://grzesiek11.stary.pc.pl/files/mkv.html</a>. From top to bottom, this is:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>MP4 with H.264 + AAC</li>\n<li>WebM with AV1 + Opus</li>\n<li>Matroska with AV1 + Opus</li>\n<li>Matroska with H.264 + AAC</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/Fyrd/caniuse/issues/7347",
            "title": "Feature request: Matroska (MKV) video container",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-30T04:44:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-16T15:01:38.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jedenastka",
                "url": "https://github.com/jedenastka"
            }
        },
