        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5131513?u=9c8c6b27565acddaba9b02f6ed26a19f79e35ebd&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Apparently, there's a proposal for adding the function import.sync(), which does what the import() function does, only synchronously. I found this by entering the query \"how to import a javascript module synchronously\" in google.com, so unfortunately, I don't know anything more. However, it's something I really need. Google also said \"This feature is not yet widely supported in browsers and Node.js.\", which seems to imply that it's somewhat supported???</p>",
